<main id="main" class="wrap web-page"><header><p class="eyebrow"><a href="web.html">Nexo Web</a></p><h1>Components and routing</h1><p class="lede">Build screens from typed components, share layout state and navigate between pages.</p><nav aria-label="Web guides"><p><a href="web-guide.html">Components and routing</a> · <a href="web-api.html">API and data</a> · <a href="web-development.html">Development</a> · <a href="web-deployment.html">Deployment</a></p></nav></header><section id="composition"><h2>Compose screens</h2><p>Components take typed, read-only scalar properties. Project imports use qualified <code>use</code> names and <code>pub</code> exports. A component projects nested content through <code>slot()</code>; a layout owns persistent shared structure. Each provider creates its own context instance; <code>inject()</code> resolves the nearest provider.</p>
<p>Pages declare explicit paths and typed parameters. Routing uses fragment URLs such as <code>#/users/7</code>, so the working demo runs on static hosting. Local anchors, back/forward navigation, nested layout persistence, page metadata, not-found and navigation error pages are supported. Navigation focuses the new page content.</p>
<p><a href="web-m2-demo/">Run the complete project</a> · <a href="web-m2-demo/source/app.nexo">Download the entry</a> · <a href="https://github.com/marcrabadan/nexo/tree/main/examples/web/composition">All project files</a>. This entry requires its <code>session.nexo</code>, <code>ui/widgets.nexo</code>, <code>ui/card.css</code> and <code>nexo.toml</code> files; it is not a standalone snippet.</p>
<p>The <a href="web-m2-demo/source/app.nexo">complete entry source</a> shows how to assemble the layout, context and pages. Download the project files together before compiling it.</p>
<p>Shared layout state survives navigation through a common layout prefix. Page state resets when leaving a page or changing parameters. Context updates batch across owners. Slots retain caller bindings and CSS, while their listeners and subscriptions are cleaned up with the receiving component.</p>
<p>Props and route parameters support <code>int</code>, <code>str</code> and <code>bool</code>. Layouts require exactly one slot and have no props yet. Local project modules/CSS are supported; package imports and SSR remain future work. Explicit keyed lists are supported. Error pages handle mount/navigation failures, not arbitrary event exceptions.</p>
<div class="code"><pre><code>python -m nexo web check --json examples/web/composition/app.nexo
python -m nexo web build examples/web/composition/app.nexo -o /tmp/nexo-composition
python -m http.server 8765 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory /tmp/nexo-composition
python -m pytest tests/test_web_frontend.py tests/test_web_composition.py</code></pre></div></section><section><h2>Scoped CSS</h2><p>Write standard CSS selectors and declarations. The compiler emits an external stylesheet with native <code>@scope</code> boundaries. Custom properties and media/container/supports queries work. Use a modern browser with CSS scope support.</p><p>Local <code>@import "./card.css";</code> is expanded into the component scope. Remote imports and resource functions such as <code>url()</code> and <code>image-set()</code>, global at-rules, CSS escapes and minification remain unsupported. Styles are component-owned; no inline style is needed.</p></section><section><h2>State and compiled markup</h2><p>Actions support typed assignments. State includes <code>int</code>, <code>str</code>, <code>bool</code> and immutable JSON records and lists. Fully constant native subtrees compile to escaped templates cloned for each instance.</p></section><section id="typed-ui"><h2>Keyed rows and typed input events</h2>
<p><a href="web-keyed-demo/">Run the working list/input example</a> · <a href="web-keyed-demo/source/app.nexo">Complete Nexo source</a> · <a href="web/technical-debt.md">Maintenance semantics and validation</a></p>
<div class="code"><div class="code-bar"><span>Typed input and row identity</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="nexo">fn edit(event: WebEvent):
    query = event.value

view:
    input(value: query, on_input: edit, aria_label: "Filter")
    ul:
        for product in products key product.id:
            li(product.name)</code></pre></div>
<p>This excerpt belongs inside a component with typed query/products state; the complete source above compiles as provided. <code>WebEvent</code> contains only frozen <code>value: str</code> and <code>checked: bool</code> snapshots. It exposes no DOM target or JavaScript methods. Input remains untrusted, and explicit assignment handlers update state. No automatic two-way binding is implied.</p></section><section><h2>Browser compatibility</h2><p>Scoped CSS relies on native <code>@scope</code>. MDN lists support from Chromium 118 and Firefox 146; Safari 26 has scoped input/textarea limitations corrected in 26.4. These feature boundaries do not establish framework or device support. Local examples are verified with system Chromium and Linux Playwright WebKit; Firefox and actual Safari/iOS qualification remain unverified. CI uses a newer pinned Firefox harness instead of the unsupported Firefox 142 bundled with Playwright 1.56.</p></section></main>
